  "narrative_llm": "<h3 class=\"story-subheading\">Short impact summary</h3>\n<p class=\"story-text\">This dataset is an early-stage scholarly output with one documented citation and one recorded downstream reuse. The available record suggests immediate relevance to research on genetically encoded voltage indicators, particularly work on imaging neuronal voltage signals.</p>\n<h3 class=\"story-subheading\">Full narrative</h3>\n<p class=\"story-text\">Optimization of Ace2N based voltage indicators was published as an open-access dataset in Figshare in 2023 and is linked to research on voltage imaging, subthreshold conduction, and related engineering and neuroscience applications. Its scholarly footprint is still small, but it already shows a clear sign of reuse: one later preprint cites the dataset as a referenced data source, indicating that the material has entered the research workflow rather than remaining only an isolated repository deposit.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">The citing work is a bioRxiv preprint on imaging neuronal voltage across the brains of larval zebrafish, which aligns closely with the dataset\u2019s technical and biological context. That connection suggests the dataset is being used in active method development for advanced fluorescence microscopy and neural activity imaging. The reuse record therefore points to a focused, domain-specific impact rather than broad dissemination at this stage.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">Usage data show only light direct engagement so far, with two recorded views and no downloads in the available DataCite record. Public attention signals are also minimal in the current archive, so the impact profile is best described as nascent and research-facing. In short, the dataset already has evidence of scholarly uptake, but the record remains too small to support any stronger conclusion about reach or standing.</p>",
